{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Cain said to Abel his brother.</b> That he recounted to him the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, and what He had said to him, and he showed him that He was strongly displeased with him, because He did not turn to him as He did to Abel. And Abel rejoiced, and Cain rose up against Abel his brother and killed him out of jealousy. And in the name of R. Joseph Kara I heard: ״ויאמר קין״ etc. — for at first he was afraid of Cain because of his anger, and guarded himself against him. And when the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, ״הלא אם תיטיב שאת״, immediately ״ויאמר קין אל הבל אחיו״ — that he told him that the Holy One, blessed be He, was reconciled to him and His anger had turned away from him. And from then on Abel thought that his mind had already cooled, and did not guard himself against going with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:20.899410206Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}